WEBVTT

1
00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:06.000
<b>In the next few verses,</b>
<b>Lord Krishna will now tell Arjuna</b>

2
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.166
<b>about the Vedic tradition-based </b>
<b>sacrifices and austerities</b>

3
00:01:11.166 --> 00:01:14.875
<b>through which divine spiritual knowledge </b>
<b>can be attained.</b>

4
00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:19.625
<b>This is the same divine knowledge that </b>
<b>will bring us close to Lord Krishna Himself.</b>

5
00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:23.500
<b>These sacrifices and austerities are in </b>
<b>accordance with the different stages,</b>

6
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:27.416
<b>circumstances, and goals of human life.</b>

7
00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:35.666
<b>These three verses are extremely important</b>

8
00:01:35.666 --> 00:01:37.291
<b>because they teach that</b>

9
00:01:37.291 --> 00:01:44.833
<b>the meaning of sacrifice is not limited to directly </b>
<b>offering ghee/materials etc. into a burning fire.</b>

10
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:49.916
<b>These verses mention different types </b>
<b>of sacrifices and austerities.</b>

11
00:01:49.916 --> 00:01:53.583
<b>Let's first understand the twenty-fifth verse.</b>

12
00:01:53.583 --> 00:02:00.541
<b>Two things are said in this verse. </b>
<b>Daivam yajñam and Brahmagnau yajñam.</b>

13
00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:04.666
<b>Daivam yajñam means worshiping deities:</b>

14
00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:08.458
<b>Some people perform worship and </b>
<b>sacrifice for goddesses/gods.</b>

15
00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:11.208
<b>Like Indra's worship for rain,</b>

16
00:02:11.208 --> 00:02:13.250
<b>Kubera's worship for wealth,</b>

17
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.125
<b>Saraswati worship for education.</b>

18
00:02:16.125 --> 00:02:22.958
<b>This sacrifice is done with the belief </b>
<b>that the deities will fulfill their material desires.</b>

19
00:02:22.958 --> 00:02:25.625
<b>This is certainly an appropriate form of sacrifice,</b>

20
00:02:25.625 --> 00:02:30.875
<b>but in the scriptures, the level of such worship</b>
<b>is considered lower than the worship</b>

21
00:02:30.875 --> 00:02:34.375
<b>and sacrifice whose purpose is </b>
<b>only to attain the Supreme Soul.</b>

22
00:02:34.375 --> 00:02:35.416
<b>The second is -</b>

23
00:02:35.416 --> 00:02:37.333
<b>Brahmagnau yajñam,</b>

24
00:02:37.333 --> 00:02:40.791
<b>meaning offering into Brahman or God:</b>

25
00:02:40.791 --> 00:02:43.791
<b>This is a different form of sacrifice and austerity,</b>

26
00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:48.125
<b>which is followed by the Jnana Yogis walking </b>
<b>on the path of knowledge.</b>

27
00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:54.333
<b>They try to engage their entire attention</b>
<b>in God or Brahman in such a way</b>

28
00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:57.791
<b>that their personality itself merges </b>
<b>into that Supreme God.</b>

29
00:02:57.791 --> 00:02:58.750
<b>Therefore,</b>

30
00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:03.666
<b>it can be seen that they are </b>
<b>offering their personality itself.</b>

31
00:03:03.666 --> 00:03:07.083
<b>Understand this with the </b>
<b>example of these two seekers:</b>

32
00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:11.208
<b>One seeker is engrossed in the </b>
<b>worship of deities in the temple</b>

33
00:03:11.208 --> 00:03:17.958
<b>and wants to obtain their blessings </b>
<b>through rituals, wants some reward.</b>

34
00:03:17.958 --> 00:03:23.541
<b>On the other hand, the other seeker is </b>
<b>absorbed only in meditation and contemplation.</b>

35
00:03:23.541 --> 00:03:29.000
<b>He is eager to understand his transcendental </b>
<b>form and the nature of the universe,</b>

36
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:37.375
<b>and through deep knowledge, he wants </b>
<b>to merge his consciousness itself into God.</b>

37
00:03:37.375 --> 00:03:40.625
<b>Now let's understand the twenty-sixth verse.</b>

38
00:03:40.625 --> 00:03:44.791
<b>This verse talks about the restraint </b>
<b>and control of the senses.</b>

39
00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:50.083
<b>In this situation, a person stops the irregular indulgence/enjoyment of the senses,</b>

40
00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:56.500
<b>or understand it as he renounces this indulgence</b>
<b>/enjoyment in the sacrifice like an offering.</b>

41
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.875
<b>Here it is mentioned in two ways,</b>

42
00:03:58.875 --> 00:03:59.750
<b>First -</b>

43
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.750
<b>the right use of the senses</b>

44
00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:03.708
<b>and second –</b>

45
00:04:03.708 --> 00:04:06.416
<b>control over the enjoyment of the senses.</b>

46
00:04:06.416 --> 00:04:12.250
<b>This is suitable for the Brahmacharya </b>
<b>Ashrama and Grihastha Ashrama of human life.</b>

47
00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:19.041
<b>The right use of the senses - A Brahmachari, </b>
<b>i.e., one who is in the education phase of life,</b>

48
00:04:19.041 --> 00:04:26.541
<b>by controlling his senses, focuses his </b>
<b>power of hearing on spiritual subjects.</b>

49
00:04:26.541 --> 00:04:31.458
<b>He listens about God and chants only His name.</b>

50
00:04:31.458 --> 00:04:37.708
<b>This control of the senses and their proper</b>
<b>use towards God is also a kind of sacrifice.</b>

51
00:04:37.708 --> 00:04:42.750
<b>A sacrifice where instead of giving pleasure </b>
<b>and enjoyment to the senses,</b>

52
00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:47.958
<b>he renounces them in the </b>
<b>fire of discipline like an offering.</b>

53
00:04:47.958 --> 00:04:51.291
<b>The second is control over the </b>
<b>enjoyment of the senses – </b>

54
00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:58.291
<b>A person who is in household life uses his</b>
<b>senses according to the rules of the scriptures. </b>

55
00:04:58.291 --> 00:05:02.666
<b>Whatever enjoyment of the senses he does, </b>
<b>he keeps it within limits.</b>

56
00:05:02.666 --> 00:05:04.125
<b>For example,</b>

57
00:05:04.125 --> 00:05:10.041
<b>in married life, he does not see physical</b>
<b>relationships from the perspective of enjoying lust</b>

58
00:05:10.041 --> 00:05:16.541
<b>but sees it as the human nature of </b>
<b>reproduction and a social duty.</b>

59
00:05:16.541 --> 00:05:19.333
<b>Whether a Brahmachari or a householder – </b>

60
00:05:19.333 --> 00:05:24.291
<b>by the right use of their senses, they </b>
<b>are performing sacrifices in different ways.</b>

61
00:05:24.291 --> 00:05:28.791
<b>Where the student walks on the path </b>
<b>of divine knowledge with full mind,</b>

62
00:05:28.791 --> 00:05:32.666
<b>the householder, instead </b>
<b>of indulging in enjoyment,</b>

63
00:05:32.666 --> 00:05:35.833
<b>renounces it and lives a life within limits—</b>

64
00:05:35.833 --> 00:05:41.500
<b>both are renunciations, both are </b>
<b>like offerings in a sacrifice.</b>

65
00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:44.416
<b>Then in the twenty-seventh verse, it is said</b>

66
00:05:44.416 --> 00:05:50.083
<b>that some people offer all </b>
<b>the actions of their senses</b>

67
00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:54.458
<b>and the actions of the life breath in the</b>
<b>fire of self-control as a sacrifice.</b>

68
00:05:54.458 --> 00:05:57.250
<b>Let's understand this.</b>

69
00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.625
<b>Here is an indication towards </b>
<b>the sacrifice of the Yogis,</b>

70
00:06:00.625 --> 00:06:04.083
<b>such as Patanjali's Ashtanga Yoga.</b>

71
00:06:04.083 --> 00:06:11.291
<b>In this Yoga, the Yogi, by controlling both </b>
<b>his breath i.e., life force and his senses,</b>

72
00:06:11.291 --> 00:06:14.416
<b>withdraws his attention from the external world</b>

73
00:06:14.416 --> 00:06:19.041
<b>and focuses it on his inner soul.</b>

74
00:06:19.041 --> 00:06:21.958
<b>Here, the Yogi is offering every </b>
<b>action of his senses,</b>

75
00:06:21.958 --> 00:06:27.625
<b>even his breath, in a way as a sacrifice </b>
<b>in the form of control.</b>

76
00:06:27.625 --> 00:06:29.833
<b>This too is a sacrifice. –</b>

77
00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:33.000
<b>In these three verses, Krishna teaches us</b>

78
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:38.375
<b>that there are many ways to perform </b>
<b>sacrifices in different life situations.</b>

79
00:06:38.375 --> 00:06:44.416
<b>Also, in that sacrifice, controlling oneself, </b>
<b>restraining one's desires </b>

80
00:06:44.416 --> 00:06:48.375
<b>is also in a way an offering of desires itself.</b>

81
00:06:48.375 --> 00:06:53.208
<b>In the scriptures, an appropriate </b>
<b>sacrifice is mentioned for everyone.</b>

82
00:06:53.208 --> 00:07:01.208
<b>The only requirement is that we understand</b>
<b>it and purify our souls by following it.</b>

83
00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:13.875
<b>These verses speak of sacred offerings, </b>
<b>austerity, sacrifice and dedication.</b>

84
00:07:13.875 --> 00:07:22.625
<b>Whenever you give up something of value</b>
<b>for a higher spiritual purpose,</b>

85
00:07:22.625 --> 00:07:27.125
<b>it becomes a form of sacred offering.</b>

86
00:07:27.125 --> 00:07:32.750
<b>You can practice these principles</b>
<b>in your personal life as well.</b>

87
00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:35.333
<b>Consider this example –</b>

88
00:07:35.333 --> 00:07:41.458
<b>Often, you may find yourself </b>
<b>deeply engaged in your professional work,</b>

89
00:07:41.458 --> 00:07:45.000
<b>experiencing continuous success.</b>

90
00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.291
<b>However, </b>

91
00:07:46.291 --> 00:07:51.791
<b>as time progresses, this success </b>
<b>demands more of your time,</b>

92
00:07:51.791 --> 00:07:55.125
<b>and gradually, your joy and </b>
<b>energy begin to diminish.</b>

93
00:07:55.125 --> 00:08:01.083
<b>Even amidst vast material success, </b>
<b>you experience an inner emptiness.</b>

94
00:08:01.083 --> 00:08:02.416
<b>In such times,</b>

95
00:08:02.416 --> 00:08:07.250
<b>if you take a portion of your earnings</b>

96
00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:15.041
<b>or carve out a few hours from your busy </b>
<b>schedule to engage in community service,</b>

97
00:08:15.041 --> 00:08:20.041
<b>such as contributing to the education </b>
<b>of underprivileged children,</b>

98
00:08:20.041 --> 00:08:25.458
<b>you'll find profound joy and fulfillment.</b>

99
00:08:25.458 --> 00:08:33.208
<b>In this transformation, you've sacrificed your </b>
<b>wealth, time, and certain material comforts –</b>

100
00:08:33.208 --> 00:08:38.666
<b>or let's say, offered them as a sacred offering.</b>

101
00:08:38.666 --> 00:08:39.375
<b>However,</b>

102
00:08:39.375 --> 00:08:44.041
<b>In return, your mind becomes pure.</b>

103
00:08:44.041 --> 00:08:47.500
<b>This becomes a form of spiritual sacrifice.</b>

104
00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:51.333
<b>This sacrifice not only purifies you</b>

105
00:08:51.333 --> 00:08:52.416
<b>but</b>

106
00:08:52.416 --> 00:08:58.166
<b>also advances you on the </b>
<b>path of spiritual progress.</b>

107
00:09:02.416 --> 00:09:09.250
<b>Life presents different situations that call</b>
<b>for different types of sacrifices.</b>

108
00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:14.250
<b>This holds true for family life as well.</b>

109
00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:16.791
<b>Let’s understand this.</b>

110
00:09:16.791 --> 00:09:18.625
<b>In family life,</b>

111
00:09:18.625 --> 00:09:20.000
<b>sacrifice</b>

112
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:27.333
<b>doesn't mean abandoning your home</b>
<b>family and everything else.</b>

113
00:09:27.333 --> 00:09:40.041
<b>Rather, it means striking a balance between </b>
<b>personal desires and family needs.</b>

114
00:09:40.041 --> 00:09:48.375
<b>Giving up some personal pleasures for </b>
<b>family welfare transforms it into a sacred act.</b>

115
00:09:48.375 --> 00:09:52.458
<b>Take the example of parents.</b>

116
00:09:52.458 --> 00:09:54.166
<b>Parents.</b>

117
00:09:54.166 --> 00:09:59.916
<b>They often sacrifice their personal </b>
<b>comforts for their family.</b>

118
00:09:59.916 --> 00:10:03.791
<b>Sometimes, instead of buying </b>
<b>something for themselves,</b>

119
00:10:03.791 --> 00:10:08.166
<b>they invest that money in </b>
<b>their children's education.</b>

120
00:10:08.166 --> 00:10:09.583
<b>During exam time,</b>

121
00:10:09.583 --> 00:10:16.958
<b>for their children's well-being, they </b>
<b>even restrict their own entertainment.</b>

122
00:10:16.958 --> 00:10:18.666
<b>There are numerous instances</b>

123
00:10:18.666 --> 00:10:26.083
<b>where, in a family setting, an individual </b>
<b>foregoes their comfort and needs,</b>

124
00:10:26.083 --> 00:10:32.166
<b>channeling them instead into </b>
<b>family love and responsibility.</b>

125
00:10:32.166 --> 00:10:34.458
<b>This too is sacrifice,</b>

126
00:10:34.458 --> 00:10:41.041
<b>a form of offering made for others' well-being.</b>

127
00:10:41.041 --> 00:10:45.250
<b>This also becomes a form of sacred duty.</b>

128
00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:53.166
<b>A sacrifice that purifies and brings </b>
<b>joy to the family atmosphere.</b>

129
00:10:57.625 --> 00:11:04.916
<b>Sacrificing something for a </b>
<b>higher purpose is sacred,</b>

130
00:11:04.916 --> 00:11:10.583
<b>and this principle will always prove valuable </b>
<b>in professional life.</b>

131
00:11:10.583 --> 00:11:12.791
<b>For professional growth,</b>

132
00:11:12.791 --> 00:11:18.083
<b>sacrifice your comfort, not your principles;</b>

133
00:11:18.083 --> 00:11:25.458
<b>sacrifice the desire for quick gains, </b>
<b>not your wisdom.</b>

134
00:11:25.458 --> 00:11:33.458
<b>Consider the example of a young employee</b>
<b>striving for professional growth.</b>

135
00:11:33.458 --> 00:11:34.625
<b>For him,</b>

136
00:11:34.625 --> 00:11:43.958
<b>Instead, the right path is to sacrifice</b>
<b>leisure time to work harder,</b>

137
00:11:43.958 --> 00:11:53.291
<b>Instead, the right path is to sacrifice</b>
<b>leisure time to work harder,</b>

138
00:11:53.291 --> 00:11:58.958
<b>learn new skills, and understand </b>
<b>new work processes.</b>

139
00:11:58.958 --> 00:12:00.333
<b>Similarly,</b>

140
00:12:00.333 --> 00:12:04.291
<b>for someone in a leadership position,</b>

141
00:12:04.291 --> 00:12:10.875
<b>it's not appropriate to constantly criticize </b>
<b>those working under them.</b>

142
00:12:10.875 --> 00:12:11.750
<b>Rather,</b>

143
00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:20.958
<b>it's proper to spare some personal time </b>
<b>to help them, to train them.</b>

144
00:12:20.958 --> 00:12:28.916
<b>By adopting this approach, you help others, </b>
<b>contribute to organizational growth,</b>

145
00:12:28.916 --> 00:12:33.541
<b>and ultimately progress yourself.</b>

146
00:12:33.541 --> 00:12:37.833
<b>In this sacred duty, everyone benefits.</b>

